          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What screening tool does guidance describe for anxiety, and what does the score change?",
          "answer": "The seven-item generalized anxiety disorder questionnaire (GAD-7) is the tool most often used for both screening for anxiety and tracking its severity.\n\nA score of 5 on the GAD-7 typically indicates mild anxiety, 10 indicates moderate anxiety, and 15 indicates severe anxiety. A score of 10 or higher is usually the point at which further assessment is recommended (Preventive services and psychiatric association guidance).\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
